# AchillesAPI v0.10.2 — Full Local Training Lab

Release date: 2026-11-07

## New in this release

- Full training API in `src/achillesapi/lab/full_app.py`, served only on loopback.
- 18 OpenAPI operations with Bearer, Basic, API key and cookie authentication.
- Deliberate BOLA, BFLA, BOPLA, mass assignment and simulated SQL error disclosure.
- Paired protected routes for comparison and safe in-memory fake fixtures.
- Input validation, nonstandard object identifiers and POST-to-GET workflow.
- OpenAPI export utility: `python -m achillesapi.lab.export_spec`.
- New local-only PowerShell startup and demo scripts.
- Optional Ollama startup/model install; first model download requires Internet.
- `auto-assess` now pairs profiles to declared OpenAPI security mechanisms.
- New plain-language Italian laboratory walkthrough.
- Dedicated tests for all lab security scenarios and OpenAPI consistency.

## Restrictions and caveats

- This lab is **deliberately insecure**. Bind only to `127.0.0.1`.
- The SQL error is a simulation: this lab does not contain injectable SQL.
- The core generic scanner still performs GET only, and will not automatically
  execute POST/PATCH/DELETE.
- The local model is not bundled. Install Ollama and download `llama3.2:3b`.
- Credentialed traffic over HTTP requires explicit `--allow-insecure-http`
  because the training API is served on local HTTP.
- Windows PowerShell startup scripts are provided but have not been run on a
  Windows host in this release validation.

## Validation

- `pytest`: 90 passed (as of final build).
- Live local HTTP smoke test using real uvicorn and CLI `auto-assess`: 33 GET
  requests sent, no demo tokens exposed in the JSON report.
- Legacy BOLA and safe SQL canary probes exercised against the local training API.
- Local Ollama inference was not tested (model not installed in this environment).
